	(lib_symbols)
	(text_box "DESIGN NOTES - ESP32-C5\n\nESP32-C5-WROOM-1-N16R8 (16 MB flash, 8 MB PSRAM, on-module PCB antenna; Wi-Fi is a backup, normally offline - Q18) as esp_hosted Wi-Fi remote (2.4 + 5 GHz Wi-Fi 6). Same module as the ESP32-C5 DevKit.\n16 MB flash: factory + 2 OTA slots so the P4 can update the C5 over SDIO (host-driven slave OTA, nice-to-have).\nSDIO to P4 on the SAME P4 pins as the reference board's ESP32-C6-MINI-1 (host firmware shared).\nC5 CHIP_PU and BOOT strap (GPIO28): open-drain from P4 AND from FT2232H ch B (DTR/RTS auto-reset).\nC5 UART0 -> buffer -> FT2232H ch B. Pin numbers from C5 datasheet (differ from C6).\nSupply 3V3_C5 (PM2 ch3). Module on the BOTTOM side with its antenna end in a board margin OUTSIDE the panel outline, at the board edge, datasheet keep-out on all layers, away from the SMA/RF edge. Fallback: WROOM-1U (u.FL).\nP4 SIDE (same as reference C6): SDIO CLK 18, CMD 19, D0-D3 14-17 with 51k pull-ups; CHIP_PU from P4 GPIO54 (0R); C5 GPIO <- P4 GPIO6 (0R, reference C6 IO2). Map to the C5's SDIO slave pins per the C5 datasheet.\nC5 PIN PLAN (ESP32-C5 datasheet v1.5): SDIO slave CLK=GPIO9, CMD=GPIO10, D0=GPIO8, D1=GPIO7, D2=GPIO14, D3=GPIO13. UART0 TX=GPIO11, RX=GPIO12.\n!! GPIO13/14 are ALSO the C5 USB_D-/D+ (USB-Serial/JTAG) - 4-bit SDIO uses them, so the C5 USB port is NOT available. Debug/flash the C5 over UART0 only.\nSTRAPS: boot mode GPIO26/27/28 (27, 28 internal pull-up). BOOT button/auto-reset = GPIO28 (low + GPIO27 high = UART download). GPIO26: add 10k pull-up (floats by default; 26=27=28=0 would select SDIO download).\nSDIO edge straps GPIO25 + MTDI: leave at defaults unless esp_hosted docs require otherwise (check). GPIO7 (= SDIO D1) is the JTAG-source strap - ignored unless eFuses burned."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
